QA-015 step 3 (seat 181480, 11:25Z): „შეხვედრა დამინიშნე ნანული მოგონილთან
ხვალ 3 საათზე." sent nothing — „set up a meeting" was not a contact verb,
so the run opened a goal, drew a plan and asked „დავიწყო?" for what the owner
had just said, and Nanuli was never asked.

Meeting verbs (დამინიშნე, დამიგეგმე, შემახვედრე; „set up / arrange /
schedule / book a meeting with") are instructions now, so D316 / §97 /
§99.5 apply as to any „ask X": no plan card, the server's send. The person
is read from the „-თან" („with") form, the meeting noun kept out of the
name; what goes to them is the line without the verb and the name
(„შეხვედრა ხვალ 3 საათზე." / „a meeting tomorrow at 3"), or just
„შეხვედრა" when nothing else is said — worded for the reader by the D711
editor like every ask. No new fixed text.

